To convert markdown text to HTML formatted in C++, you can use an external library such as `cpp_markdown`. Here's a function that accomplishes this:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <cpp_markdown.h>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& mdText) {
    cpp_markdown::MarkdownDocument mdDoc(mdText);
    std::string html = mdDoc.ToText();
    return html;
}

int main() {
    std::string mdText = "### Title";
    std::string htmlText = markdownToHtml(mdText);
    std::cout << "Markdown: " << mdText << std::endl;
    std::cout << "HTML: " << htmlText << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This function uses the `cpp_markdown` library to convert the input Markdown text to HTML. The `cpp_markdown::MarkdownDocument` object is initializes with the Markdown text, and its ToString() method is called to performs the actual conversion. The result is then returned as a `std::string`.

To compile this code, you need to link the `cpp_markdown` library. The Github page is available at: https://github.com/cpp-markdown/cpp-markdown. Make sure you have it available in your environment or include it in your build system.

